      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hot flashes: many clinicians start w an SSRI, then consider adding gabapentin or megestrol; medroxyprogesterone is reserved for the most severe, intractable cases; SSRIs (listed: venlafaxine, fluoxetine, paroxetine, sertraline): moderate efficacy and quite safe, but less effective than progesterone."
